"[Background Fetch] Preserve CORS parameters on download retry and fix null
response crash" (crbug 574059465; no CVE listed yet): when a Background
Fetch download was interrupted and resumed, its fetch mode, credentials
mode, initiator, isolation info and URL loader factory were lost, so a
cross-origin retry reverted to navigation mode and bypassed CORS; and a
download failing before its response headers crashed on a null response.
chromium/src main commit 40142acee843ca4531d1cb2851a311ca8f64e478
(main@{#1730715}), merged on 2026-10-30 to 158 and to 157 as
40158475f2b69b773f4d29a8f4fb79c30c1af9ca (refs/branch-heads/8103@{#1003},
after the 157.0.8103.33 tag); not proposed for 156. This is the 157 merge,
without its tests. Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

